  "source": "I1",
  "what": "Task 2: the first and last pad of every connector row on the 0.1 inch pitch that runs across the board (x) with at least eight pads, marked on I1 for the board's x scale. The rule was set before any of them was fitted: every such row, and the rows of the DIPs that lie across (IC74 and IC75, from the scale section), and nothing else; the rear sockets (SK1 to SK7) are on their own pitches (SK6, a D socket, is on 2.77 mm) and are not used. The pitch count is the pads counted on a 1:2 view of each connector with a 20 px grid, and agrees with the row's length in pixels at 2.54 mm. board_frame.py moves each mark to the centroid of the solder blob nearest it (common.refine_to_pad), refusing a move over 0.6 mm, and finds every pad between them the same way."
 },
