  "source": "I1",
  "what": "The centres of the four corner pins of each DIP footprint: pins 1, N/2, N/2 + 1 and N in some order, named by where they lie in the scan (tl, tr, bl, br: top left, top right, bottom left, bottom right). Which corner is pin 1 does not matter to the scale. The pin count is the one a row's length in pixels allows at the 2.54 mm pitch (the next count up or down is 2.54 mm, about 40 px, away). spike.py moves each mark to the centroid of the solder blob nearest it (common.refine_to_pad), and refuses the move when that centroid is over 0.6 mm from the mark."
 },
